{
    "version": "0.4.0",
    "description": "Tray monitor for AI coding-agent token usage, cost, and subscription quota. Windows port of TokenBar.",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/Nanako0129/Syrtis-Windows",
    "license": "MIT",
    "notes": [
        "Syrtis is managed by Scoop here, not by its own installer. Update it with",
        "`scoop update syrtis`.",
        "",
        "If the in-app 'Check for updates' button reports a failure, that is expected",
        "on a Scoop install and nothing is broken - that button talks to the",
        "installer's own update feed, which does not manage this copy. It is not the",
        "update path here either way.",
        "",
        "If you turn on Launch at login, the registry entry it writes points at this",
        "Scoop directory and is left in place on uninstall. It does nothing while the",
        "app is gone, and starts working again by itself if you reinstall, because",
        "Scoop's path stays the same. Remove it by hand from Task Manager's Startup",
        "tab if you would rather it were not there.",
        "",
        "Usage data lives in %APPDATA%\\tokscale and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\TokenBar, outside",
        "the Scoop directory, so it survives updates and is left behind on uninstall."
    ],
